<article class="env-lemma" id="08AS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08AS">Lemma <span data-tag="08AS">69.20.3</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $f : X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ be a proper morphism of algebraic spaces. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Then $H^ i(X, \mathcal{F})$ is finite $A$-module for all $i \geq 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is just the affine case of Lemma <a href="/tag/08AR" data-tag="08AR">69.20.2</a>. Namely, by Lemma <a href="/tag/0720" data-tag="0720">69.3.1</a> we know that $R^ if_*\mathcal{F}$ is a quasi-coherent sheaf. Hence it is the quasi-coherent sheaf associated to the $A$-module $\Gamma (\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A), R^ if_*\mathcal{F}) = H^ i(X, \mathcal{F})$. The equality holds by Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/0733" data-tag="0733">21.14.6</a> and vanishing of higher cohomology groups of quasi-coherent modules on affine schemes (Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01XB" data-tag="01XB">30.2.2</a>). By Lemma <a href="/tag/07UB" data-tag="07UB">69.12.2</a> we see $R^ if_*\mathcal{F}$ is a coherent sheaf if and only if $H^ i(X, \mathcal{F})$ is an $A$-module of finite type. Hence Lemma <a href="/tag/08AR" data-tag="08AR">69.20.2</a> gives us the conclusion. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>